Quoted legal source texts carry their own terms, recorded per vendored encoding
row in subjects/<path>/<subject-id>/encodings/<encoder>/SOURCE-LICENSE.md (see
docs/directory-conventions.md §4.1). A pointer row records no terms here: the
encoding it indexes lives in another repository and carries its own.

Attributions required by those terms are collected here as subjects land:

  sg/pdpa-2012 — Singapore Personal Data Protection Act 2012, and the PDPC
  Advisory Guidelines. The applicable source terms are UNDETERMINED; see that
  subject's SOURCE-LICENSE.md. No attribution is recorded because none has yet
  been established, not because none is required.

  sg/penal-code-1871 — Singapore Penal Code 1871, section 301, published by the
  Attorney-General's Chambers on Singapore Statutes Online. The applicable
  source terms are UNDETERMINED, on the same open question as sg/pdpa-2012; see
  that row's SOURCE-LICENSE.md. Unlike sg/pdpa-2012 this encoding reproduces its
  section VERBATIM rather than paraphrasing it, which is a material difference
  for whatever assessment settles the question. No attribution is recorded
  because none has yet been established, not because none is required.

  us/chubb-hospital-cash — the first row here whose terms are DETERMINED rather
  than undetermined, and therefore the first that records a real attribution
  rather than an open question. The synthetic policy encoded in this row is
  Appendix A, "ILLUSTRATION 1: SUPPLEMENTAL HOSPITALIZATON CASH POLICY", of:

      Oliver R. Goodenough & Preston J. Carlson, "Words or code first? Is the
      legacy document or a code statement the better starting point for
      complexity-reducing legal automation?" (2024). PMC10894687.
      https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10894687/

  That article is distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License
  (CC BY 4.0), http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ — verified against
  the PMC full text on 2026-08-31. The encodings quote the policy inline (inert
  style), so this attribution discharges a licence CONDITION and must not be
  removed.

  The text actually encoded is a modified variant printed at arXiv:2502.17638
  Appendix A.1, which carries arXiv's non-exclusive distribution licence and
  does not itself cite Goodenough & Carlson for the policy. We rely on the CC BY
  grant above, not on that paper. See the row's SOURCE-LICENSE.md for what that
  distinction does and does not settle.
